      "restore_edits": [
        {
          "start": 2,
          "end": 3,
          "lines": [
            "This file is a human-readable view of `project/Config/FixedRollBallLayout.json`. It does not add gameplay requirements. `GDD.md` Section 6 defines acceptance, and the JSON file supplies the exact machine layout required there.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "GDD.md",
      "published": "GDD.md",
      "sha256": "f2da09a78df9a03f3ec3a36c69716ec89d021ff5390ae85f5f161ada709d0259",
      "published_sha256": "12df8d731f92a22fa950861a92ead94fd626aab9214d604d2e853b4b90b792a3",
      "restore_edits": [
        {
          "start": 42,
          "end": 43,
          "lines": [
            "| Project entry | `project/RollBallStarter.uproject` opens with Unreal Engine 5.7.4. | `QUALITY-01` |\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 49,
          "end": 50,
          "lines": [
            "| Observation bridge | The public bridge reports `provider_ready=false` and `game_state=null`. | Engineering contract in `contracts/README.md` |\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 175,
          "end": 180,
          "lines": [
            "| `LAYOUT-01`, `LAYOUT-02` | `project/Config/FixedRollBallLayout.json` | Yes | Defines the fixed maze, start, exit, walls, and trap locations. | No; this exact layout data is the benchmark fixture. |\n",
            "| `LAYOUT-01` | `project/Content/StarterContent/Architecture/Floor_400x400.uasset` | Yes | Supplied solid 3D board tile for safe floor cells. Its three-dimensional thickness and shading must remain visible in play. | No; use the supplied mesh. |\n",
            "| `LAYOUT-01`, `LAYOUT-02`, `HAZARD-01` | `project/Content/StarterContent/Architecture/Floor_400x400_Hole.uasset` | Yes | Supplied 3D trap tile with a visible center opening and safe surrounding rim. The rim and opening must remain distinct in the playable view. | No; use the supplied mesh. |\n",
            "| `LAYOUT-01` | `project/Content/StarterContent/Architecture/Wall_400x200.uasset` | Yes | Supplied 3D board wall for the fixed maze boundaries, with visible height above the floor. | No; use the supplied mesh. |\n",
            "| `MOVEMENT-02` | `project/Content/StarterContent/Shapes/Shape_Sphere.uasset` | Yes | Supplied 3D sphere mesh used for the player-controlled ball, with readable volume, lighting, and rolling rotation. | No; use the supplied mesh. |\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "INITIAL_AGENT_PROMPT.md",
      "published": "INITIAL_AGENT_PROMPT.md",
      "sha256": "dbc925d0eb99cc34ebe3bb2709fd73dbbc40a6e59f427278caf0b7dba07bb0fc",
      "published_sha256": "a9ea7e5c8f63878cad4b37a8da99c0a78fc51264ec6c9ffe30018b78118a91fa",
      "restore_edits": [
        {
          "start": 8,
          "end": 9,
          "lines": [
            "Read the public files in the exact order listed in `README.md`. `GDD.md` Section 6 is the sole gameplay acceptance authority.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 12,
          "end": 13,
          "lines": [
            "Before handoff, set `GameDefaultMap` and `EditorStartupMap` in `project/Config/DefaultEngine.ini` to the project-owned playable map you created. Leaving the starter value `/Engine/Maps/Entry` launches the inert preview and makes an Alt+P smoke check appear to do nothing. Verify one Alt+P (or the documented public runtime command) after a successful build, then record the observed window and map in your handoff.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 16,
          "end": 18,
          "lines": [
            "- Start from `project/RollBallStarter.uproject` and deliver through the same project entry.\n",
            "- `project/` is the only writable input root.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 32,
          "end": 33,
          "lines": [
            "Implement the player results in `GDD.md` while preserving reasonable implementation freedom. Normal keyboard input must reach all required gameplay. Keep the fixed layout and trap positions supplied in `project/Config/FixedRollBallLayout.json`, and use the supplied board, trap-hole, wall, and ball meshes in their required visible roles; do not replace them with primitives or hidden substitutes.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 34,
          "end": 35,
          "lines": [
            "Retain and extend the read-only transport defined by `contracts/README.md`. The starter reports `provider_ready=false`; the completed candidate must publish schema-valid snapshots with `provider_ready=true` to the launcher path supplied through `-RollBallStatePath`. This transport is evaluator interoperability, not a gameplay control path, and it must never mutate the game.\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "start": 42,
          "end": 43,
          "lines": [
            "Before handing off, leave the best runnable candidate in `project/`. Report the checks actually run and their outcomes, the final project entry, incomplete or unverified requirement IDs, and any build, runtime, tool, or environment fault. Do not invent scores, token counts, step counts, package validity, or evaluator results.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
